{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 105, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 2->3 is already absent, removing edge 1->3 leaves only the direct 0->3 path (or none), collapsing the network, as in exp #4 (-52 on C10)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1->3 missing, node 3 depends heavily on edge 0->3, so removing it risks disconnection, as in exp #62 (-61 on C10)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the 0->3 edge, deleting 2->3 can leave node 3 nearly or fully cut off, as in exp #20 (-61 on C10)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0->2 is absent, node 1 is the only route to node 2, so removing 0->1 kills both intermediate nodes, as in exp #60 (-77 on C10)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling on 1->3 with a 3x3 conv adds real capacity (exps #74, #86 gave about +4 on IN16), while replacing another conv gains little."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on the 0->3 edge is a well-known strong choice when it replaces a blurring avg pool (exps #53, #57 positive), but it loses capacity when it replaces a conv (exp #35 negative)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Dropping the 3x3 conv on the final 2->3 edge removes the main learned transformation (exps #6, #26, #36 all strongly negative), unlike replacing a pool (exp #41 positive)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a pool for a conv on the 1->2 edge adds parameters and helps clearly (exps #42, #75), while swapping from none or another conv is roughly neutral."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on 0->2 with a pool throws away capacity (exp #50, -5 to -10), more than replacing a skip or none."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing an avg pool on 0->1 with a skip helps consistently (exps #5, #68, #78), whereas replacing a 3x3 conv with a skip hurts (exp #30)."}], "tok": 17049, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [4, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [4, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [0, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [2, "none"]], [["none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [1, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [2, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none"], [1, "nor_c